AiTask daily_monthly_booking_count_slack_summary {
  label: 'Daily Monthly Booking Count Slack Summary'
  description: 'Creates a fresh summary of booking counts by check-in month from @Dashboard:homestay_performance_statement and posts it to #hoa every day.'

  brief: @md
    Review the **Monthly Booking Count by Check-in Month** visualization in @Dashboard:homestay_performance_statement. Run it with fresh data, then write a concise Slack-ready summary of booking counts by check-in month.

    Include:
    - The check-in month range represented and booking count for each available month.
    - The highest- and lowest-booking months, including their counts. Treat ties explicitly.
    - A short trend observation only when supported by the monthly series; do not infer causes.

    Deliver the completed summary to the Slack channel #hoa using the available AI delivery capability. Use a clear title and compact bullets. Do not attach a dashboard export unless it is necessary to communicate the result.

  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - The summary is based on a fresh execution of the Monthly Booking Count by Check-in Month visualization in @Dashboard:homestay_performance_statement.
    - It reports the available check-in months and their booking counts accurately, and identifies the highest- and lowest-booking month or tied months with their counts.
    - Any trend statement is supported by the monthly series and does not assert an unsupported cause.
    - A concise, readable version of the completed summary is delivered to Slack channel #hoa via the available AI delivery capability.
    - No values, trends, or delivery status are invented.
  ;;
}